Depends: passwd, ffmpeg
Recommends: redis-server
Suggests: postgresql | mariadb-server, nginx | caddy
Description: Self-hosted team chat, files and video meetings
 MeetHub is a team chat with channels, direct messages, threads, file
 attachments and video meetings (through LiveKit), served by one static
 binary with the web app embedded.
 .
 Everything is installed in /opt/meethub and runs as the meethub user under
 systemd (meethub.service). It needs a Redis server; the database is SQLite by
 default, or MariaDB or PostgreSQL. Meeting recordings are composed with the
 distribution's ffmpeg.
